  "summary_en": "European Parliament resolution of 3 May 2022 adopting the AIDA Special Committee report. It reviews AI in health, the Green Deal, security, competitiveness, democracy and labour, compares the EU with the US and China, and sets a roadmap for risk-based, human-centric AI regulation, standards, sandboxes and investment. It calls for an international ban on lethal autonomous weapons.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Supports a risk-based, technology-neutral, harmonised EU legal framework for AI, with regulations as the legal form",
   "Calls for regulatory sandboxes, EU standards and certification or labelling to build trust",
   "Reiterates a call for an international ban on lethal autonomous weapons and for meaningful human control over lethal force",
   "Urges more investment, skills, data spaces and infrastructure to close the gap with the US and China",
   "Requires human oversight and safety by design in high-risk AI to counter automation bias"
  ],
